lican nominee, could quickly move this race.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wisconsin remains one of the most evenly divided states in the country, and the 2028 presidential race there is an open contest with no incumbent on the ballot. No general-election polls or expert ratings have been published yet, so the outlook rests on the state's fundamentals, which point to a dead-even race.\n\nRecent coverage highlights a volatile cycle: contested primaries in both parties, questions about polling reliability in battleground states, and debate over the Republican field, with commentary criticizing Tom Tiffany as an extremist. None of this yet provides a clear directional signal, leaving the race a genuine tossup with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.498, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4982, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5145, "margin": 0.5}]}